I> scope := ABI9001.named.natural.integer|bool record signedness only
  + CSSLv3.HIR→MIR→Cranelift.{object,JIT} + focused.native witnesses.
N! Apocv4 | canonical.profile-six | Graphify | deploy | merge mutated.

§P defect
  ✓ MIR integer types erase source signedness.
  ✓ ABI9001 layout retained width+offset but not signedness.
  ✓ constructor therefore admitted same-width iN↔uN substitutions.
  ✓ projection returned signless MIR without reseeding canonical
    `integer_unsigned_values`; cast|shift|division|remainder|ordered-relation
    could select signed lowering for projected unsigned high-bit values.
  ✓ direct-MIR metadata previously admitted self-consistent overlapping layout.

§D repair
  1. `MirStructLayout.field_integer_unsigned` parallels declaration-order fields:
     Int→Some(true=unsigned|false=signed) ; Bool→None ; invalid shape→refusal.
  2. HIR named-layout construction stores declared width+signedness.
  3. record constructor requires exact field name+MirType+signedness provenance;
     contextual integer literal receives declared type; mismatch|unknown refuses.
  4. constructor MIR carries exact `field_signedness` CSV.
  5. projection resolves registered field, emits `field_signedness`, and restores
     Int provenance into `integer_unsigned_values`.
  6. integer cast|right-shift|ordered-relation consume restored provenance.
  7. integer division|remainder now require exact equal widths+signedness and
     select {divsi,divui,remsi,remui}; unknown|mixed contracts fail closed.
  8. Cranelift object+JIT validate operation metadata against registered nominal
     layout: identity, field names/count, natural offsets, widths, signedness,
     storage, byte order, operand/result types, projection-operand nominal type.
  9. direct-MIR numeric `named(...)` without signedness rejects; forged Bool
     signedness rejects; raw scalar projection cannot spoof nominal identity.

§D refusal.contract
  MIR.codes += {
    ABI9001-SIGNEDNESS-CONTRACT-UNVERIFIED,
    ABI9001-FIELD-SIGNEDNESS-CONTRACT-UNVERIFIED,
    ABI9001-FIELD-SIGNEDNESS-MISMATCH
  }.
  MIR.op += `cssl.integer.divrem.contract.unverified`.
  backend.code := ABI9001-MALFORMED-METADATA.
  ✓ i8↔u8 + i16↔u16 + i32↔u32 + i64↔u64 constructor flips refuse.
  ✓ Bool admits only field.type=Bool + integer.contract=None.
  ✓ unregistered|pathless|overlap|nonnatural|metadata-sign-flip|scalar-spoof refuse.
  ✓ nested|float|pointer|size3|size>8 remain outside ABI9001 admission.
  ✓ legacy.native-x64 nominal-record refusal remains; backend parity N! claimed.

